# Paths exempt from the .githooks/pre-push scan, one path prefix per line.
#
# This file covers ATTRIBUTION METADATA ONLY: published author/contributor and
# license attribution that is meant to be public, so it is never "scrubbed" by
# accident. Fixture/user/path privacy goes through the `pii-allow` line marker
# (and the ALLOW_USERS list in .githooks/pre-push), not through this file.
#
# The two scanner files are listed because they carry the secret/PII signatures
# verbatim (denylist literals, `sk-ant-`, `github_pat_`, `_authToken`, the
# mailto domain rule); scanning a signature file for its own signatures is a
# guaranteed false positive on every push that touches it.
.secrets.patterns
.githooks/pre-push
.secrets.allowlist

# Attribution metadata that is published on purpose (upstream maintainer
# contact, license headers): the attribution class per this file's charter.
package.json
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
LICENSE
# Scanner-signature carriers: pre-push-gate.ts embeds the credential regexes
# (github_pat_ et al.) as its blocklist - same self-reference class as
# .secrets.patterns / .githooks/pre-push above.
src/main/pre-push-gate.ts
# Synthetic fixture carrier: persistence tests carry a fake sk-ant- key in an
# envVars string literal (pii-allow cannot be retro-marked inside a rewritten
# historical diff; the value is synthetic by construction).
src/renderer/state/persistence.test.ts
src/main/pre-push-gate.test.ts
